<title>SINGAPORE: QAF nine months net profit S$8.56 mln.</title>
<headline>QAF nine months net profit S$8.56 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>				9-mth   vs     12-mth to March 31 1996</p>
<p>    Net profit	    8.56    vs     13.25</p>
<p>    Dividend (cts)	1.2     vs	1.6</p>
<p>    Group shr   (cts)   2.7     vs	4.2</p>
<p>    Group shr diluted   2.6     vs	3.9</p>
<p>    Turnover	    237.05    vs    371.30</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		13.44    vs     21.37</p>
<p>    Tax		     4.87    vs	6.32</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gain  0.20    vs	1.23 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - QAF Ltd said its core business of food manufacturing, retailing, trading and catering contributed to 99 percent and 76 percent of turnover and pre-tax profit respectively.</p>
<p>The company has changed in its financial year end to December 31 from March 31 to bring it in line with its parent company, the Salim Group of Indonesia.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
